chorus-endpoint: the chorus Linux endpoint
===========================================

What is installed:

  /usr/bin/chorus-client                          the endpoint
  /usr/lib/systemd/system/chorus-client.service   runs it (not enabled on install)
  /etc/chorus/client.conf                         its arguments (a conffile)
  /usr/bin/chorus-verify-host                     the host contract and the spin test
  /usr/lib/chorus/verify-host, /usr/lib/chorus/probe
                                                  what chorus-verify-host runs
  /usr/bin/chorus-wakeup-probe                    the wakeup-jitter probe

To start it:

  1. Edit /etc/chorus/client.conf: the endpoint's name, its zone, the server's
     address, the ALSA device (`aplay -L` lists them).
  2. sudo systemctl enable --now chorus-client
  3. journalctl -u chorus-client -f

Before turning real-time playout on in client.conf, run chorus-verify-host
with the service's limits (the command is at the top of
/usr/bin/chorus-verify-host).

The repository's docs/linux-endpoint.md is the full install page.
